body:
GREG, 2026-11-26, relayed by Engram::Asistant (mailbox 43498a6e), on the Windows B coding plan:
- about 17:32Z, #2112, verbatim: „Chwila!! Powien byc engram”;
- #2114, verbatim: „Po to mamy sync engram. + Kimi. Dlatego robimy te toole.”;
- EXPLICIT WORD, 17:46Z, #2124 (message 86b6fb34), verbatim: „Tak dla Engram na Window B.” It answers the joint question Fable #2122 / Fable2 #2864, which asked for:
  - creating the local store C:\Users\Greg\.engram on Windows B;
  - enabling task sync and importing tasks and memories from engram-data;
  - enabling the Engram MCP integration for the Engram AND TermAl projects on Windows B.
Background: the explicit word was needed because session-8's Claude Code classifier refused `engram init` and session-12 (Codex) refused under AGENTS.md "changing user or global configuration ... needs Greg's explicit word". Neither refusal was bypassed.
SCOPE, per Asistant #2116: this set-up only, NOT standing consent for every future Windows B install. It covers:
- the Engram binary install there: release build of master bc0628b6, installed at C:\Users\Greg\.cargo\bin\engram.exe, build fdaead5a916e, schema d2859de61cfc, the same schema and rev as Central;
- the store, the task-sync join and the per-project TermAl integration for both projects;
- coding sessions (Opus or Codex gpt-6.2-sol, effort high).
Claims are LOCAL to each host's store and never transfer; synced task text and memories do. Assign work so that one item is not executed on two hosts.
